# Relational Database Standards

Enforcement: **B**. Pair with the specific engine file under `engines/`.

## Schema

- Primary keys: stable, unique; prefer opaque IDs when business keys change.
- Foreign keys enforce integrity when supported and affordable at write path.
- Unique constraints for natural uniqueness; partial uniques when the engine allows.
- Check constraints for simple domain invariants at the DB when appropriate.

## Transactions & isolation

- Know the engine’s default isolation level.
- Keep transactions short; no remote calls inside transactions.
- Document required isolation (e.g. avoid dirty reads for money paths).
- Be explicit about lock contention risks on hot rows.

## Indexing

- Index for measured query paths; every index costs writes and storage.
- Avoid redundant indexes; consider covering indexes only when proven.
- Review `EXPLAIN` / equivalent before “optimizing.”

## Anti-patterns

- SELECT * in hot paths
- Unbounded result sets without pagination
- ORM N+1 ignored under load
- Wide transactions updating many unrelated rows
